    "final_text": "Both features are added, and `npm test` passes (59 tests, including the new ones).\n\n- **`edit <id> <text>`**:\n  - It replaces the text and keeps the id, completed status and `createdAt`. The text is trimmed, as `add` does.\n  - A missing id, a missing or blank text, or an unknown id prints `Error: \u2026` to stderr, exits with 1 and leaves `todos.json` unchanged.\n  - Multi-word text has to be quoted, the same as `add`.\n- **`list --pending`**: shows only incomplete todos in the same format as `list`. Plain `list` still shows everything.\n\n**Choices I made:**\n- When nothing is pending, `list --pending` prints `No pending todos.`.\n- `list` with any flag other than `--pending` is an error.\n- I updated the usage text and the README examples.\n\nThe logic is in `src/todos.js` and `src/cli.js`, and the new tests are in `test/edit-pending.test.js`. I haven't committed anything.",
